    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter tonight\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** serving as the clear offensive anchor, sporting a 73.42 efficiency score. His favorable lead-off spot against Dotel provides the requisite volume to hunt for the stolen bases necessary to maintain our competitive edge in that category. Similarly, **Josh Smith** is a high-upside play tonight; despite hitting seventh, his favorable dynamic platoon matchup against Bassitt boosts his profile to 64.66, making him a high-efficiency contributor who effectively leverages the SP\u2019s 4.77 xERA. While **Trea Turner** and **Junior Caminero** are facing elite arms in Sale and Ullola respectively, their talent floor remains high enough to warrant starts, though their output will likely rely on raw skill rather than situational advantages tonight.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved **Chase Meidroth**, who finished just outside the starting nine with a 54.14 score. While his lead-off positioning offered a compelling case, his matchup against Liberatore lacked the same volatility or park-induced upside that favored **Hector Rodriguez** or **Josh Smith**. We have opted to bench **Dillon Dingler** entirely, as his 39.24 score falls below the Zebras' 40.0 floor; his negative dynamic platoon split against Adams makes him a liability in a category-dependent Roto format where efficiency per plate appearance is paramount. We continue to monitor the status of **Yordan Alvarez**, who remains sidelined, keeping our bench depth essential for navigating these late-season rotations. \n\nManagers should remain wary of the heavy platoon tax affecting **Carson Benge** today; his 48.31 score is tempered by an unfavorable L/L matchup against Rod\u00f3n, and he should be monitored closely for an early hook if the Zebras look to preserve plate appearance caps. While **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** and **Kazuma Okamoto** both face favorable SP profiles against Scherzer and Bassitt, their lower spots in the order limit their scoring ceilings. With no significant weather threats reported, the priority remains maximizing stolen base opportunities from **Pete Crow-Armstrong** and **Caleb Durbin** to keep the team in striking distance in our scarcest category.",
